WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.190
With Fifty Shades Of Grey out now, let’s
take a look at 25 things you probably didn’t

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:08.200
know about the big-screen version of E.L.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:09.800
James’s erotic novel!

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:15.610
In order to keep the Fifty Shades Of Grey
script top-secret, during early auditions,

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:18.240
actors were asked to prepare a scene from
another film.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:23.160
Jamie Dornan, who plays Christian Grey, chose
a scene from the 90s movie True Romance, which

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.390
was written by Quentin Tarantino.

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:32.750
For her Fifty Shades audition, Dakota Johnson
read a four-page monologue from the 60s psychological

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:36.480
drama Persona, which was written and directed
by Ingmar Bergman.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:40.800
Johnson’s performance of this particular
piece allowed the filmmakers to see she was

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:46.620
capable of bringing to life Ana’s emotional
journey in Fifty Shades Of Grey.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:51.200
Jamie Dornan has said the scene he most enjoyed
filming was the first time that Christian

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:55.870
and Ana meet, which the filmmakers shot over
two days.

00:00:55.870 --> 00:01:00.310
To help them develop a believable mother-daughter
bond, Dakota Johnson, who plays Ana, and Jennifer

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:04.890
Ehle, who plays Ana’s mother, would chat
on the phone while Johnson was on set and

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:06.060
Ehle was at home.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:10.799
The actresses found this particularly helpful
as most of Ana and her mother’s communication

00:01:10.799 --> 00:01:14.060
takes place over the phone.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:19.219
Fifty Shades Of Grey was shot in the Canadian
city of Vancouver, which doubled for the book’s

00:01:19.219 --> 00:01:24.899
setting in the US cities of Seattle and Vancouver
in Washington State, and Portland, Oregon.

00:01:24.899 --> 00:01:30.740
And although the story is set in summer, filming
actually took place in winter.

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:35.759
The filmmakers kept the details of what they
were filming and where as quiet as possible.

00:01:35.759 --> 00:01:40.420
They did this to avoid roads and streets becoming
crowded with onlookers which could have led

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:43.799
to expensive delays to their tight production
schedule.

00:01:43.799 --> 00:01:48.609
Use of the title Fifty Shades Of Grey was
banned on set and in any correspondence or

00:01:48.609 --> 00:01:51.109
printed materials connected with the film.

00:01:51.109 --> 00:01:55.350
Instead, the crew used the fake name The Adventure
Of Max And Banks.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:02:00.739
Max is the name of EL James’s dog, and Banks
is the name of screenwriter Kelly Marcel’s

00:02:00.739 --> 00:02:01.739
puppy.

00:02:01.739 --> 00:02:06.759
There were 55 locations in the movie’s final
shooting schedule.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:12.860
The Fairmont Hotel in Vancouver, Canada, doubled
for the Heathman Hotel in Portland, Oregon,

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:17.470
while the University of British Columbia stood
in for Washington State University.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:22.420
Ana and Christian’s first date at a coffee
shop was filmed in the Gastown district of

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:25.180
Vancouver, Canada, which doubled for Portland.

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:30.709
Ladner Village Hardware, which is located
in a small town about 45 minutes from Vancouver,

00:02:30.709 --> 00:02:37.280
was chosen to represent Clayton’s Hardware
Store, where Ana works while in college.

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:41.940
When production designer David Wasco first
met with director Sam Taylor-Johnson, the

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:46.609
pair discovered they’d each, independently,
chosen the same photograph as a reference

00:02:46.609 --> 00:02:49.540
shot for the tone and look of Fifty Shades
Of Grey.

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:55.000
The photograph was by fashion photographer
Helmut Newton, from his book White Women.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.170
Author E.L.

00:02:57.170 --> 00:03:02.359
James drew a floor plan of Christian’s penthouse
to help production designer David Wasco get

00:03:02.359 --> 00:03:08.040
to grips with the layout of Christian’s
home in the Fifty Shades trilogy.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:12.569
Two Vancouver houses built a quarter of a
mile apart for entrepreneurial brothers in

00:03:12.569 --> 00:03:15.019
the 1920s feature in the film.

00:03:15.019 --> 00:03:19.590
To make sure they gave the homes the right
look for the story’s setting, the movie’s

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:22.770
design team researched upper-end Seattle homes.

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:26.400
One of the Vancouver homes was used for the
exterior of Christian’s family residence,

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.670
as well as its foyer and dining room.

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:33.180
While the second home was used for its glass-enclosed
swimming pool, which appears instead of the

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:36.219
book’s boathouse.

00:03:36.219 --> 00:03:40.030
Sets were built for Christian’s penthouse
including the living room, kitchen, dining

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:44.140
room, his bedroom, Ana’s bedroom, and, of
course, the Red Room.

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:48.781
They concealed the sets by building them on
stages so preventing people from seeing them.

00:03:48.781 --> 00:03:53.010
The whole build covered three stages.

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:57.799
To create the look of Christian’s penthouse,
the filmmakers used as a point of reference

00:03:57.799 --> 00:04:03.279
the work of architects including Norman Foster,
John Parson, and Hugh Newell Jacobsen.

00:04:03.279 --> 00:04:09.709
Thanks to her background as an artist, director
Sam Taylor-Johnson was able to secure paintings

00:04:09.709 --> 00:04:15.939
by artists including Ed Ruscha and John Baldessari
to display in the offices of Christian Grey.

00:04:15.939 --> 00:04:20.840
The work of many other artists also appears
in the film, as does one of the director’s

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:22.900
own pieces.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:26.949
The most challenging and revealing scenes
between Christian and Ana were kept till the

00:04:26.949 --> 00:04:27.949
end of the shoot.

00:04:27.949 --> 00:04:32.710
So, the scenes in Christian’s infamous Red
Room were shot during the last two weeks of

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:33.979
filming.

00:04:33.979 --> 00:04:39.169
Dakota Johnson wanted her reaction to the
Red Room to be as genuine as possible, so

00:04:39.169 --> 00:04:43.990
the very first time she saw it was when her
character Ana sees it for the first time in

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:45.259
the movie.

00:04:45.259 --> 00:04:50.699
To heighten the impact of the Red Room, the
filmmakers limited the use of red and black

00:04:50.699 --> 00:04:55.620
in the movie, except for graduation gowns
at Washington State University’s graduation

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:57.870
ceremony.

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:03.250
To make sure they got the look of the Red
Room just right, production designer and set

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:08.379
decorator David and Sandy Wasco consulted
the experts, in other words, dominatrices

00:05:08.379 --> 00:05:10.000
with Christian Grey-type clients.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:14.789
One of the things they discovered was that
leather is the best floor covering because

00:05:14.789 --> 00:05:16.590
of all the kneeling people do.

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:17.599
Author E.L.

00:05:17.599 --> 00:05:22.979
James was quite specific about the room’s
layout and director Sam Taylor-Johnson was

00:05:22.979 --> 00:05:25.180
quite particular about its appearance.

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:30.770
For example, Taylor-Johnson wanted the room
to reference high-end stables, so the design

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:35.400
team went for brown leather and wood equipment
as opposed to the black often favoured in

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.400
such rooms.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:42.750
Much of the furniture and equipment seen in
the Red Room was custom-made in England.

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:47.790
To research his character Christian Grey,
Jamie Dornan visited a sex-dungeon to watch

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:51.629
a session between a dominant and a submissive.

00:05:51.629 --> 00:05:56.310
A great deal of care was taken over the design
of Christian Grey’s clothes.

00:05:56.310 --> 00:06:01.139
The filmmakers discussed issues such as the
type of cuffs, collars and lapels, the weight

00:06:01.139 --> 00:06:03.770
of the fabric, and the amount of patterning.

00:06:03.770 --> 00:06:08.389
All but one of the suits worn by Jamie Dornan
were handmade, and all his shirts were also

00:06:08.389 --> 00:06:09.389
custom-made.

00:06:09.389 --> 00:06:11.360
And if there’d been enough time, his footwear
would also have been bespoke, but all his

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:12.360
shoes were still top-of-the-line.

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:16.930
Costume designer Mark Bridges was very specific
about Christian’s ties, their thickness,

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:19.389
their sturdiness and, of course, how grey
they were!

00:06:19.389 --> 00:06:24.129
All of Christian’s infamous silver ties
were specifically designed and painstakingly

00:06:24.129 --> 00:06:26.690
handmade.

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:31.740
Costume designer Mark Bridges designed a peach
silk and chiffon dress for Ana which echoes

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:37.650
an iconic dress worn by Faye Dunaway in the
1968 film The Thomas Crown Affair.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:39.790
Author E.L.

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:44.700
James set a challenge for the movie’s property
master Dan Sissons for the scene where Christian

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:48.000
and Ana share champagne after her graduation.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:52.780
James showed Sissons a photo of a pair of
antique teacups she owns and asked him if

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:55.479
he could find them or something similar for
the scene.

00:06:55.479 --> 00:07:00.160
The cups are actually over one hundred years
old and the company that made them no longer

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:06.880
exists, but Sissons managed to track down
six identical cups, which arrived on set just

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:11.210
48 hours after his conversation with James!

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:16.629
Christian Grey has Audi’s latest fleet of
cars at his disposal including the R8 sports

00:07:16.629 --> 00:07:22.590
car, the S8 sedan cruiser, and the brand new
A3, which he gives Ana as a gift.

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:28.830
Although the latest model A3 wasn’t available
to buy until after filming ended, the filmmakers

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:31.990
managed to secure it for their shoot.

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:39.780
Christian’s EC130 helicopter, Charlie Tango,
is the largest helicopter that may be privately

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:41.830
owned and costs around $2 million!

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:48.360
For the movie, the art department fully customised
the EC130 including its graphics so they fit

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:53.240
the designs found elsewhere in Christian’s
professional world.

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:58.300
Sam Taylor-Johnson directed the music video
for “Earned It”, by Canadian singer-songwriter

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:01.420
The Weeknd, which features in Fifty Shades
Of Grey.

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:06.259
The music video features Dakota Johnson and
the work of Fifty Shades Of Grey cinematographer

00:08:06.259 --> 00:08:07.650
Seamus McGarvey.

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:12.490
Well there you have it, 25 things you probably
didn't know about Fifty Shades Of Grey!

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:16.370
Now, tell me, what’s your favourite big-screen
adaptation?

